  "chapter": 428,
  "signer": "KATHY HOCHUL",
  "text": "\n \n                APPROVAL MEMORANDUM - No. 20 Chapter 428\n \n      MEMORANDUM filed with Assembly Bill Number 4587-A, entitled:\n \n    \"AN ACT to amend the general obligations law, in relation to exclud-\n        ing  certain seasonal use tenancies from the provisions regulat-\n        ing deposits and advances for residential dwelling units\"\n \n    APPROVED\n \n  This bill will exclude certain seasonal use tenancies from  provisions\nlimiting  security  deposits  to  one month. To be applicable, the lease\nmust expressly provide that the unit is registered  as  a  seasonal  use\nunit, the occupancy must not exceed one hundred and twenty days, and the\ntenant  must have a primary address to return to. The dwelling unit must\nalso register with the appropriate local  government,  county  or  state\nregistry  as a seasonal use dwelling. Finally, such dwelling unit cannot\nbe rented as a seasonal use dwelling for more than one hundred and twen-\nty days per year.\n \n  I agree with the intent of this bill, which will  carve  out  seasonal\nrentals  from  the limitation of security deposits to one month rent and\nprovide for governmental oversight. As written, the bill envisions  that\nboth  the localities and the State will be able to set up a registry for\nlandlords to take advantage of this exemption. However, localities typi-\ncally oversee land recording issues and are best positioned  to  monitor\nseasonal  use  tenancies,  not  the  State. Therefore, I have reached an\nagreement with the Legislature to ensure that it  is  local  and  county\ngovernments that will operate the registries contemplated by this legis-\nlation.\n \n  With these agreed upon changes, I am pleased to sign this bill.\n \n  This bill is approved.                         (signed) KATHY HOCHUL\n\n                                ______\n",
  "year": 2021
 },
